@amd-maradosa Thanks for normalizing the config. `smem_estimation`, the pinned `mm_configs` entry, and `exceeds` now all come from the post-`_filter_configs` object, so on ROCm the assertions compare against the `num_stages` the kernel actually compiles with. The dedup on the collapsed stage axis is a good addition.

I updated the PR description to cover the normalization and the upstream `blackwell_ws_persistent_tma_mm_template` rename. I also noted that the gfx1151 numbers in the Test section were measured before the normalization. If you re-run at head, feel free to replace them.

